.Dd October 14, 2026
.Dt DEV-SECRET 1
.Os macOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm dev-secret
.Nd keep developer secrets in a dedicated macOS keychain and expose them per command
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm init
.Op Fl -defaults Ar file
.Nm
.Cm set
.Ar NAME
.Op Fl -stdin
.Nm
.Cm get
.Ar NAME
.Nm
.Cm run
.Ar NAME ...
.Fl -
.Ar command
.Op Ar arg ...
.Nm
.Cm list
.Nm
.Cm delete
.Ar NAME
.Nm
.Cm keychain
.Cm lock | unlock | status
.Nm
.Cm keychain biometric
.Cm enable | disable | status
.Nm
.Cm doctor
.Nm
.Cm scan-env
.Op Ar file ...
.Nm
.Cm import-env
.Op Fl -yes
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
stores tokens and passwords in a dedicated keychain instead of plaintext shell
rc files, and hands them to a single command as environment variables only when
asked.
It is a thin wrapper around
.Xr security 1
and has no other dependencies.
.Pp
Secret names must be valid environment variable names
.Pq Li [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]* .
Every command that reads or writes secrets unlocks the keychain first, with
Touch ID if enrolled, otherwise with the keychain password.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm init Op Fl -defaults Ar file
Create the dedicated keychain, add it to the user keychain search list, and
create the config directory.
Offers Touch ID enrollment when available.
Safe to run again.
.It Cm set Ar NAME Op Fl -stdin
Store a secret, replacing any existing value.
Prompts twice without echo, or reads the value from standard input with
.Fl -stdin ,
removing trailing newlines and carriage returns.
Any other byte is stored and returned exactly.
.It Cm get Ar NAME
Print a secret to standard output.
Prefer
.Cm run ,
which never puts the value in your terminal or shell history.
.It Cm run Ar NAME ... Fl - Ar command Op Ar arg ...
Run
.Ar command
with each named secret set in its environment.
The secrets are not exported to the calling shell.
Exits with the command's exit status.
.It Cm list , Cm ls
Print stored secret names, one per line.
Values are never printed.
.It Cm delete , Cm rm Ar NAME
Delete a secret.
.It Cm keychain lock | unlock | status
Lock or unlock the dedicated keychain, or show its settings.
.It Cm keychain biometric enable | disable | status
Manage Touch ID unlock.
See
.Sx SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS .
.It Cm doctor
Check that the environment has what
.Nm
needs.
.It Cm scan-env Op Ar file ...
Report lines in shell rc files that assign plaintext values to variables whose
names contain TOKEN, SECRET, PASSWORD, PASS or KEY.
Values are never printed.
.It Cm import-env Oo Fl -yes Oc Op Ar file ...
Move the values found by
.Cm scan-env
into the keychain and replace each line with a comment.
A backup of every changed file is written next to it with mode 0600.
Assignments that use command substitution are reported and left alone.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev DEV_SECRET_KEYCHAIN_NAME
Keychain name.
Default:
.Li dev-secrets .
.It Ev DEV_SECRET_KEYCHAIN_PATH
Keychain file.
Default:
.Pa ~/Library/Keychains/$DEV_SECRET_KEYCHAIN_NAME.keychain-db .
.It Ev DEV_SECRET_CONFIG_DIR
Default:
.Pa ~/.config/dev-secret .
.It Ev DEV_SECRET_DEFAULTS_FILE
Default:
.Pa $DEV_SECRET_CONFIG_DIR/defaults .
.It Ev DEV_SECRET_SERVICE_PREFIX
Prefix of each keychain item's service name.
Changing it hides previously stored secrets.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/Library/Keychains/dev-secrets.keychain-db
The dedicated keychain.
.It Pa ~/.config/dev-secret/
Config directory, mode 0700.
.It Pa ~/.config/dev-secret/.biometric-enabled
Present when Touch ID unlock is enabled.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Cm run
exits with the status of the command it runs.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Store a token, then use it for one command:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dev-secret set GITHUB_TOKEN
dev-secret run GITHUB_TOKEN -- gh auth status
.Ed
.Pp
Store a value produced by another tool:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gh auth token | dev-secret set NODE_AUTH_TOKEN --stdin
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr security 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Simone Andreani
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Secrets and the keychain password are passed to
.Xr security 1
on standard input, not as arguments, so they do not show in
.Xr ps 1 .
Values longer than about 1.9 KB are the exception and
.Cm set
warns about them.
.Pp
While the dedicated keychain is unlocked, any process running as your user can
read its items.
Touch ID unlock stores the keychain password in the login keychain, readable
without a prompt, so it is a convenience rather than a security boundary.
See
.Pa docs/THREAT_MODEL.md
in the source repository.
